  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Oxfam in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT Donor Visit in Vietnam
24-26 January 2024
Soc Trang Province in Mekong Delta of Vietnam

Objectives of the visit:
&#x2022; To provideopportunities for SCR implementing partners in Vietnam and the project Donor to dialogue update on project SCR progress, practical opportunities and challenges for project execution.
&#x2022; To create space for open interaction between the donor and the project beneficiaries so that the donors not only understand the quality and quantity of impacts but also understand local operational context of the project.
&#x2022; Build common understanding and discussion with Oxfam Mekong PMU and, and Oxfam in Vietnam management team about SCR project progress, key issues and way forward.

Expected outcome:
&#x2022; SCR management team and funding partner(s) have chance to visit project site, hear, learn from SCR implementing partners, and riverine communities and share our appreciation and accepting with more understanding about the local context in Mekong Delta.
&#x2022; All actors in SCR project built stronger relationships and be able to discuss some project opportunities, challenges, and next steps.
&#x2022; Increased understanding and knowledge about SCR&#x2019;s project management, and partnership approach in Vietnam in order to provide necessary support to the Vietnam team.

List of visitors (see Annex 2 for details):
&#x2022; Vietnam Dykes and Disaster Management Authority (VDDMA), Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development (MARD);
&#x2022; DFAT from Vientiane post: 3 persons
&#x2022; Oxfam Mekong Program Management Unit: 3 persons
&#x2022; Oxfam in Vietnam: 3 persons</narrative>
  </description>
